{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"uncommon-floatable-chamois","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Context\nA reviewer advisory on Gerrit change 3054 (story 7300, landed as commit 35ca10e501b). Deleting the real-tree subprocess tests left a module-level constant that nothing reads:\n- tests/unit/test_check_ssm_secret_state.py:25  `GATE = REPO_ROOT / \"scripts\" / \"check_ssm_secret_state.py\"`\n- tests/unit/test_check_templatefile_escapes.py:23  `GATE = REPO_ROOT / \"scripts\" / \"check_templatefile_escapes.py\"`\nA grep confirms 1 occurrence of `GATE` in each file, its definition. Neither is flagged by ruff (module-level constants are not F841).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Neither file defines `GATE`, and neither imports or uses anything that only `GATE` needed (checked: `git grep -n -w GATE -- tests/unit/test_check_ssm_secret_state.py tests/unit/test_check_templatefile_escapes.py` prints nothing; `ruff check` on both files is clean).\n- [ ] Both modules still collect the same tests (checked: `pytest --collect-only -q` node counts before and after are equal).\n- [ ] `make verify` shows no failure outside the known pandoc set, and the Gerrit change is `Verified +1`.\n","id":"9cbd-35ea-c2bd-4197","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Remove the unused GATE constants left in two check-script test modules"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792975130678976001,"uuid":"e1f43941-3ace-4d0a-adb8-a4cb47865694"}